{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-29T21:07:15.677Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Summary of changes:\n\n**Task 1: `renameBranch` through the Vcs port**\n\n- `src/core/vcs/vcs.ts`: added `renameBranch(from, to): Promise<void>` after `createBranch`, with a one-line doc comment.\n- `src/core/vcs/git-vcs-merge.ts`: added `renameBranch(ctx, from, to)` running `git branch -m` and throwing `combined(result)` on failure.\n- `src/core/vcs/git-vcs.ts`: delegates `renameBranch` to the merge helper; parsers moved out (249 → 209 lines).\n- `src/core/vcs/git-vcs-parse.ts` (new): holds `nonEmpty`, `parseStashBranch`, `parseStashes`, `parseStatus` unchanged; exports the three `git-vcs.ts` uses.\n- `src/core/vcs/no-vcs.ts`: `renameBranch` calls `this.reject()`.\n- `tests/vcs-write.test.ts`: `PORT_MEMBERS` now lists `renameBranch` (only test change).\n- `tests/vcs-rename-branch.test.ts` (new): rename keeps commits, taken name fails changing nothing, `NoVcs` fails naming git off.\n\nBoth verifies pass (`node --import tsx --test tests/vcs-rename-branch.test.ts` and `pnpm verify`). Result written to `openspec/changes/117-approve-after-halt/.run/results/1.md`."}}
